roke=\"#f2c79b\" stroke-width=\"6.3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/></g><g class=\"kdaR\"><line x1=\"164.9\" y1=\"156.7\" x2=\"171.8\" y2=\"177.4\" stroke=\"#f2c79b\" stroke-width=\"6.3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/></g><g class=\"kdhd\"><circle cx=\"150\" cy=\"133.7\" r=\"16.1\" fill=\"#4a3520\"/><circle cx=\"150\" cy=\"137.2\" r=\"14.9\" fill=\"#f2c79b\"/><g class=\"kdey\"><circle cx=\"144.8\" cy=\"134.9\" r=\"2.2\" fill=\"#1f2937\"/><circle cx=\"155.2\" cy=\"134.9\" r=\"2.2\" fill=\"#1f2937\"/></g><path d=\"M145.4 141.8 q4.6 5.2 9.2 0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#1f2937\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/></g></g><g class=\"cp1\"><rect x=\"40\" y=\"214\" width=\"158\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" fill=\"#cfe3ff\"/><text x=\"119\" y=\"243\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#17428f\" class=\"sb\">The girl</text></g><g class=\"cp2\"><rect x=\"212\" y=\"214\" width=\"246\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" fill=\"#ffe0c2\"/><text x=\"335\" y=\"243\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#8a3d0f\" class=\"sb\">kicked the ball</text></g><g class=\"cp3\"><rect x=\"472\" y=\"214\" width=\"130\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" fill=\"#e6dbff\"/><text x=\"537\" y=\"243\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#52309c\" class=\"sb\">end mark .</text></g><g class=\"cpp\"><circle cx=\"636\" cy=\"236\" r=\"19\" fill=\"#c8f7d0\"/><path d=\"M627 236l6 6 12-15\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#15803d\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/></g><text x=\"360\" y=\"298\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#334155\" class=\"st\">Read it aloud: it feels finished.</text></g></svg>",
        "alt": "Animated cartoon: a girl walks in a sunny park and kicks a ball that arcs across the scene while The girl, kicked the ball and the end mark build up in order; the sun spins, clouds drift and a tick appears.",
        "caption": "A living cartoon sentence: watch the girl kick the ball as the sentence assembles itself."
      },
      "example": "The girl kicked the ball.\nWho or what? The girl. Did what? Kicked the ball. It makes complete sense, so it is a sentence.\n\nIt rained.\nThis is also a sentence. It is short, but it tells one complete idea.\n\nThe tall girl with the red shoes.\nThis is not a sentence. It tells us who, but it never says what she did.",
      "notice": "Common mistake: believing a long group of words must be a sentence. Length does not make a sentence. A complete idea does.",
      "check": {
        "question": "What does a complete sentence need?",
        "options": [
          "A picture and a title",
          "Someone or something and what they did, told as one complete idea",
          "At least ten words"
        ],
        "correct_index": 1,
        "explanation": "A sentence tells one complete idea. It needs a who or what part and a doing or being part."
      }
