idth=\"290\" height=\"152\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#ffe0c2\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"556\" y=\"214\" width=\"120\" height=\"44\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#f3d9b1\"/><path d=\"M548 214 L616 168 L684 214 z\" fill=\"#c94f4f\"/><rect x=\"632\" y=\"178\" width=\"26\" height=\"26\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#bfe3ff\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><g class=\"wl\"><circle cx=\"645\" cy=\"191\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#fbbf24\"/></g><rect x=\"596\" y=\"176\" width=\"22\" height=\"44\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><text x=\"545\" y=\"242\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#8a3d0f\" class=\"sb\">we stayed inside</text><path d=\"M322 132 h76\" stroke=\"#16a34a\" stroke-width=\"6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"><animate attributeName=\"stroke-dasharray\" values=\"0 80;80 0;80 0\" keyTimes=\"0;.6;1\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/></path><g class=\"so\"><circle cx=\"360\" cy=\"132\" r=\"30\" fill=\"#dcfce7\" stroke=\"#16a34a\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"360\" y=\"140\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"21\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#166534\" class=\"sb\">so</text></g><text x=\"312\" y=\"120\" font-size=\"28\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#166534\">,</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"264\" width=\"560\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\"/><text x=\"360\" y=\"288\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#166534\" class=\"sb\">and adds an idea   |   but shows a contrast   |   so shows a result</text></g></svg>",
        "alt": "Animated cartoon: rain falls from a drifting cloud and a puddle ripples, a house window glows, and a green bridge with the word so and a comma joins the two cards.",
        "caption": "Watch the rain fall and the bridge form. The word so shows that the rain caused staying inside."
      },
      "example": "It was raining, so we stayed inside.\nSo shows the result: the rain caused staying inside.\n\nI wanted to play, but it was too dark.\nBut shows a contrast.\n\nWe packed a picnic, and we drove to the beach.\nAnd simply adds another idea.",
      "notice": "Common mistakes: using and to join two ideas that are not really related, and leaving out the comma before and, but or so when they join two complete ideas.",
      "check": {
        "question": "Which joining word best completes: The path was slippery, ___ we walked slowly.",
        "options": [
          "but",
          "so",
          "and"
        ],
        "correct_index": 1,
        "explanation": "Walking slowly was the result of the slippery path, so so is the best choice."
      }
    },
    {
      "icon": "🌈",
      "title": "Adding clear detail",
      "explain": "A short sentence can be clear and correct, but detail helps the reader picture what you mean. Useful detail answers one of four questions: when, where, how, or what kind. For example, the plain sentence The dog ran becomes clearer as After lunch, the brown dog ran across the park.\n\nBuild detail one piece at a time. Start with a complete sentence, then add a single piece of detail and read the whole sentence again. If it still says one clear idea, add another piece. Keeping the main idea easy to find is more important than making the sentence long.\n\nA when phrase that comes at the start of a sentence takes a comma after it, as in After lunch, the dog ran. Too many describing words can bury the main idea, so check that every detail earns its place and helps the reader.",
